.TH GIT-PR-SUBMIT 1 "2026-08-10" "git-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-pr-submit \- submit default-branch commits through a pull request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git pr-submit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git pr-submit
turns local commits made directly on the repository default branch into a
GitHub pull request, queues protected squash auto-merge, and returns the
checkout to the default branch.
.PP
The worktree must be clean, the current branch must be the repository default,
and the exact remote default-branch commit must be an ancestor of the local
head. Behind or divergent branches are rejected rather than rebased
automatically because conflict resolution must remain an explicit user action.
.PP
The command snapshots and fetches the exact remote default-branch ref through a
URL validated against the current GitHub repository. It creates a deterministic
.B pr/<short-oid>
branch at the submitted head before atomically restoring the local default
branch with an expected-old-object check. This ordering ensures every later
failure leaves the submitted commits reachable on a named branch.
.PP
For one commit, its subject is the pull request title and its body is the pull
request description. For two or more commits, the Git editor is opened before
any branch is changed. The buffer contains all full commit messages in
chronological order. Its first edited line becomes the title and its remainder
becomes the body. A failed editor, unchanged normalized content, or an empty
title cancels without moving refs or creating a pull request.
.PP
Pull request creation delegates to
.BR git-pr-open (1),
which validates the push target, pushes the exact head object, and verifies the
created pull request topology. Auto-merge is requested with the same immutable
head object ID and never uses administrator bypasses, so branch protection,
required checks, and required reviews remain authoritative.
.PP
When repository auto-merge is unavailable, including on a plan-limited private
repository, creating the pull request remains a successful submission and a
diagnostic identifies the required manual landing.
If GitHub rejects auto-merge after creating the pull request, the command prints
the pull request URL, returns to the default branch, and exits nonzero. If pull
request creation itself fails, the generated branch remains checked out for
inspection or a manual
.B git pr-open
retry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The pull request was created. Auto-merge was queued when the repository allows
it.
.TP
.B 1
Repository inspection, ref movement, pull request creation, auto-merge, or
checkout recovery failed. Diagnostics distinguish failures that occur after a
branch or pull request has already been preserved.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or local repository state is unsuitable for submission.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-pr-open (1),
.BR git-pr-checks (1),
.BR git-pr-land (1),
.BR git-cleanup-repo (1)
